          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Working with Fractions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.08,
            0.847,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " kg of flour is used to make 12 rotis, how much flour is used to make 6 rotis?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.149,
            0.848,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Pāṭīgaṇita, a book written by Sridharacharya in the 9th century CE, mentions this problem: “Friend, after thinking, what sum will be obtained by adding together "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 \\div \\frac{1}{6}   ,   1 \\div \\frac{1}{10}   ,   1 \\div \\frac{1}{13}   ,   1 \\div \\frac{1}{9}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 \\div \\frac{1}{2}''"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What should the friend say?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.263,
            0.848,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Mira is reading a novel that has 400 pages. She read "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the pages yesterday and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the pages today. How many more pages does she need to read to finish the novel?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.351,
            0.848,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. A car runs 16 km using 1 litre of petrol. How far will it go using "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2   \\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " litres of petrol?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.408,
            0.848,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Amritpal decides on a destination for his vacation. If he takes a train, it will take him "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 \\frac { 1 } { 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hours to get there. If he takes a plane, it will take him "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hour. How many hours does the plane save?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.499,
            0.848,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Mariam’s grandmother baked a cake. Mariam and her cousins finished "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{4}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the cake. The remaining cake was shared equally by Mariam’s three friends. How much of the cake did each friend get?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.582,
            0.772,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Choose the option(s) describing the product of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\frac { 5 6 5 } { 4 6 5 } } \\times { \\frac { 7 0 7 } { 6 7 6 } } \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": ">   { \\frac { 5 6 5 } { 4 6 5 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "< \\frac { 5 6 5 } { 4 6 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": ">   { \\frac { 7 0 7 } { 6 7 6 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "<   \\frac { 7 0 7 } { 6 7 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (e) > 1 (f) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "< 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.722,
            0.639,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. What fraction of the whole square is shaded?"
